# CITATION.cff — citation metadata for GSBot (academia / research reuse)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GSBot or its architecture in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "GSBot: A Neurosymbolic Pareto-Optimal Garment Sustainability Bot for Triple-Bottom-Line Fashion and Textiles Decision Support"
abstract: >-
  GSBot (the Garment Sustainability Bot) is an open-source neurosymbolic
  (Kautz-6) chat and dashboard for fashion and textiles specialists,
  delivering materials-science and engineering-grade sustainability
  analysis across environmental (water, carbon, energy, chemicals,
  biodegradability), social (fair labour, safety, transparency) and
  economic (price-per-wear, durability-weighted cost) axes. It exposes
  Pareto-optimal non-dominated trade-off surfaces, a detachable
  assembly panel for swappable ecological-vs-economic bill-of-materials
  recomputation, an open-standards catalogue/safety feed backbone (RSS,
  Atom, ActivityStreams 2.0, schema.org, GS1, Open Apparel Registry,
  ECHA REACH), a stable C-ABI verification seam for SPARK/Ada, and a
  pilot of the Eclexia domain language on top of a verisimdb/kyaml
  core target.
type: software
